  "notes": "\"More chordal than most trap\" is the sentence this file is built on, and it shows up in two numbers no other entry in this batch carries. `extensions` is 0.28 triad / 0.50 seventh / 0.22 ninth — the research says \"7th and 9th extensions on the pads\" — against Waka's 0.88 triad at the other end of the same genre; and every progression family is four chords long, both of the ones the research names by number (i–VI–III–VII and i–iv–VI–V), with `harmonicRhythm` never reaching `vamp`. The 808 \"interacts with a pad root rather than replacing it\", which is authored as register: [21, 38] is the A0–D2 the research states, the highest 808 floor in the batch, so the pad has room underneath it. \"Sung hook in a light tenor with melisma\" is `articulation: legato` over `densityPerBar` [4, 8] with a stepwise interval split. \"Occasional double-time hat section under the hook\" is the weighted `base`, which reaches `8T` about a third of the time rather than sitting there. ⚠ `confidence` is `medium`: the research says the trap-R&B construction is clear from the catalog but workflow sourcing is thin. INFERRED: every velocity figure, the rimshot perc density standing in for \"snappy layered claps and rimshots\", the slide rate, and the whole `intervals`/`contour` split. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
